---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Work | Eshin Griffith"
  description="Selected work by Eshin Griffith across AI voice systems, TypeScript and AWS platforms, enterprise ETL, and open-source Effect tooling."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="prompt"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span> cat work.log</p>
    <h1>Selected work</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      I lead backend and platform work where product decisions, system design,
      and production operations meet. These are a few representative systems
      and open-source projects.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="work-stack">
    <article class="panel case-study" aria-labelledby="alina-heading">
      <header class="case-header">
        <div>
          <p class="panel-label">ChiroHD · AI voice scheduling</p>
          <h2 id="alina-heading">Alina</h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Alina technologies">
          <li>TypeScript</li>
          <li>AWS</li>
          <li>ElevenLabs</li>
          <li>OpenAPI</li>
        </ul>
      </header>

      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          As Alina’s primary technical decision-maker, I lead four engineers
          and coordinate across product, go-to-market, support, and executive
          teams. We advanced a hackathon prototype into a SKED-integrated voice
          scheduling product serving chiropractic offices in production.
        </p>
        <p>
          I built a reusable TypeScript and AWS platform around generated
          OpenAPI clients and namespaced ElevenLabs reconciliation. Robust,
          versioned agent and configuration deployments now take about 30
          seconds, making it possible to redeploy the fleet in minutes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Production quality is measured as well as observed: the voice-agent
          suite grew from 32 to 84 passing scenarios across six workflows,
          catching prompt and tool regressions that previously required nuanced
          manual testing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="metric-grid">
        <div class="metric">
          <strong class="metric-value">~45</strong>
          <span class="metric-label">enabled offices</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <strong class="metric-value">~60</strong>
          <span class="metric-label">agents</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <strong class="metric-value">1,000–1,500</strong>
          <span class="metric-label">monthly calls</span>
        </div>
        <div class="metric">
          <strong class="metric-value">549</strong>
          <span class="metric-label">production Step Function runs · 99% success</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="panel case-study" aria-labelledby="kollacode-heading">
      <header class="case-header">
        <div>
          <p class="panel-label">Kollacode · enterprise data systems</p>
          <h2 id="kollacode-heading">
            <a href="https://kollacode.com">Kollacode</a>
          </h2>
        </div>
        <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="Kollacode technologies">
          <li>TypeScript</li>
          <li>Node.js</li>
          <li>ETL</li>
          <li>OpenAPI</li>
        </ul>
      </header>

      <div class="case-copy">
        <p>
          At Kollacode, I led development of EDIT, an enterprise ETL platform
          processing more than 6,000 data loads annually for IBM Marketing. The
          platform reduced processing time from eight hours to 30 minutes.
        </p>
        <p>
          Other work ranged from moving client-side data processing into Web
          Workers—cutting latency from minutes to milliseconds—to building an
          automated REST documentation generator that converts TypeScript types
          into JSON Schema for OpenAPI.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section aria-labelledby="open-source-heading">
      <p class="prompt"><span aria-hidden="true">$</span> ls ./open-source</p>
      <h2 id="open-source-heading">Open-source systems</h2>
      <div class="panel-grid open-source-grid">
        <article class="panel">
          <p class="panel-label">TypeScript · Effect</p>
          <h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/egriff38/effect-herdr">effect-herdr</a>
          </h3>
          <p>
            A typed Effect SDK for a terminal-native agent multiplexer. I fixed
            seven reproduced protocol and schema defects, expanded the typed RPC
            surface from 14 to 62 operations, and removed a redundant RPC round
            trip with regression coverage.
          </p>
          <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="effect-herdr outcomes">
            <li>14 → 62 operations</li>
            <li>7 defects fixed</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="panel">
          <p class="panel-label">TypeScript · Effect · GraphQL</p>
          <h3>
            <a href="https://github.com/egriff38/effect-graphql"
              >effect-graphql</a
            >
          </h3>
          <p>
            A prototype code-first GraphQL layer over Effect Schema and RPC. I
            also published authorization and testing guides through its
            integrated documentation site.
          </p>
          <ul class="tag-list" aria-label="effect-graphql focus">
            <li>prototype</li>
            <li>authorization</li>
            <li>testing</li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .work-stack {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4rem);
  }

  .case-study {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .case-header {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    align-items: start;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }

  .case-header h2,
  .panel h3 {
    margin: 0.2rem 0 0;
  }

  .case-copy {
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .case-copy p:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .case-copy p:last-child,
  .panel p:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .open-source-grid {
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  section > h2 {
    margin-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 42rem) {
    .case-header {
      display: block;
    }

    .case-header .tag-list {
      margin-top: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
